{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794045957,"nonce":"bWXTSA0IxYHQojiH56Pt97ywH54=","message":"**SIMD and window ownership**\n\nSIMD: ashui uses ash-simd in two places, both behind -D ash_simd with a plain fallback: ashui.draw3d.BcEncoder (u8x16 min/max/splat/ge/sub through ash.simd.Vec) and canvaskit GltfPose (matrix multiplication). The user says Rayzor's SIMD is compile time like Ash's, and GPU compute through rayzor.gpu is also available. Rayzor's std has rayzor.SIMD4f/SIMD4i32/SIMD8i32/SIMD16i8/SIMD32i8 and Ptr loads. Plan: add a -D ashui_rayzor branch beside the ash_simd one using these types, and consider GPU compute for the bulk work (BC texture encoding is a natural fit).\n\nWindow: the user asked for the xwindow work to go to Rayzor. rayzor-a3 (compiler/LSP session) declined: committed to HXX completion latency for the RayDE demo, and a peer's relay is not enough for them to start; the user must assign it. Facts from them: rayzor/window is a hand-written crate (cocoa, win32, x11, web, wasm_exports, event); the Haxe side is compiler/haxe-std/rayzor/window/{Window,WindowStyle,EventType,Key}.hx, package rayzor.window, hand-written, not generated. A generated xwindow package named window (as hlwindow uses) would not collide with it. The package name is the owner's decision. Owner of window/ and the plugin ABI: unknown. Needs the user to name a session.","files":null}]}